================================================================================
FREE FOR EVERYONE — EXPERIMENTATION, RESEARCH, AND SMALL PRODUCTION
================================================================================

You may use, modify, and distribute this software FREE OF CHARGE — including
in production — under the AGPL-3.0 terms below, UNLESS you meet the commercial
trigger conditions defined in the next section.

This means individuals, students, researchers, startups, and companies of any
size can experiment, prototype, evaluate, and run this in production without
paying anything, as long as the AGPL copyleft requirements are satisfied (i.e.,
you share modifications under the same license).

================================================================================
COMMERCIAL LICENSE REQUIRED — LARGE CORP PRODUCTION USE
================================================================================

You MUST obtain a paid commercial (MIT-style) license if ALL THREE of the
following are true simultaneously:

  1. Your organization has 100 or more full-time-equivalent employees, AND

  2. You are running this software in a PRODUCTION environment — meaning it
     is processing real traffic, real user requests, or real data as part of
     a live system, product, or service (not a dev/staging/test environment,
     not a proof-of-concept, not internal experimentation), AND

  3. That production use provides direct or indirect commercial value to your
     organization (i.e., it protects a revenue-generating AI product or
     pipeline, or is offered as part of a paid service).

If you are a large company evaluating this, running it in staging, testing it
internally, using it for research, or building a one-off PoC — you do NOT need
a commercial license. Go nuts. Only pay when you ship it to production at scale.

A commercial license grants MIT-style permissions with no copyleft requirements:
use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, sublicense, and sell.

To obtain a commercial license:
  → https://github.com/brandy-savage/hot-potato/issues (open a licensing issue)
  → licensing@brandy-savage.dev

Pricing scales with org size. The bigger you are, the more this is rounding
error on your AI security budget. Startups get a steep discount. We're not
trying to shake down small teams — just the ones with actual infrastructure.

================================================================================
WHY
================================================================================

Security tools should be accessible. A solo researcher or a 5-person startup
should be able to protect their AI pipelines without paying a license. But if
a Fortune 500 is running this in front of their production LLM to protect a
product that generates millions in revenue, they can chip in. That money funds
continued development and keeps the project maintained.

We're not going after experimenters. We're going after the procurement budget
of companies that would otherwise buy a $200k/year vendor solution for this.

